Polymath combines the locally modified pdfcraft, wordcraft, gridcraft, deckcraft and lightcraft projects by Storytold and their contributors. All five original engines, formats, contributor credits and required notices are retained.

The Polymath application shell, folded-aperture icon and workspace symbols are original contributions, licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0. Native file-dialog, print, clipboard, audio and local-folder adapters are adapted from those permissively licensed sibling projects.

Full upstream license texts, third-party font and artwork attribution, and required notices are included inside Polymath.app/Contents/Resources/licenses, grouped by source repository. The source checkouts remain in ../reader, ../writer, ../sheets, ../slides and ../lightcraft. Lightcraft's trademark artwork in its docs/brand folder is not used as Polymath branding.

Local dictation bundles whisper.cpp and a converted OpenAI Whisper model under their MIT licenses. Their notices are in Contents/Resources/licenses/whisper. PDF narration uses macOS voices already installed on the user's machine.

The native interface includes an egui 0.36 compatibility port of egui-shadcn 0.5.0 by FerrisMind, MIT licensed. Its source and license are in vendor/egui-shadcn; the license is also included in the application bundle.

The macOS quit path uses craft-quit from Storytold craft-libs at commit a01382de4f5415b5a7a9133093be47c9488c1b6b, licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0. Its license texts are in assets/licenses/craft-quit and the application bundle.
